{"format":1,"key":"zone:lochmodan","path":"/lore/zone/lochmodan","name":"Loch Modan","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"lochmodan","name":"Loch Modan","path":"/lore/zone/lochmodan"},"levels":"Levels 10-20","description":"The Stonewrought Dam holds Loch Modan's great lake above the Wetlands. Around Thelsamar, troggs threaten the southern valleys while kobolds work the…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:lochmodan","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["The Stonewrought Dam holds Loch Modan's great lake above the Wetlands. Around Thelsamar, troggs threaten the southern valleys while kobolds work the mines and ogres hold the northeast highlands.","Loch Modan's lake fills a green valley east of Dun Morogh. Pines and birches climb toward the rugged peaks, while the Stonewrought Dam spans the northern rim. The dwarven town of Thelsamar draws mountaineers, hunters, and miners. Copper and tin veins run through the surrounding hills.","Broken catapults and ballistae on the lake bed recall the Second War, when the orcish Horde occupied Loch Modan before the dwarves drove them out. More recently, dwarven excavations opened underground chambers and released savage troggs. Trogg tribes, led by chieftains, have overrun the southern canyons of Stonesplinter Valley and the Valley of Kings. The Ironforge Mountaineers fight to defend the trade routes."],"hash":"fc5017","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"68b7e57a2b","sec":53},"female-narrator":{"sha":"517c203f30","sec":55}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Loch Modan (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Loch_Modan_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Loch Modan","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Loch_Modan"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/thelsamar","n":"Thelsamar","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/stonewrought-dam","n":"Stonewrought Dam","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/dunmorogh","n":"Dun Morogh","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/wetlands","n":"Wetlands","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/m